====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|Australia}} A transportable building with single rooms, often used on remote work sites or as tourist accommodation.
#* '''2004''', Susie Ashworth, Rebecca Turner, Simone Egger, ''Western Australia'', Lonely Planet, [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=QHsF6Jh7DrIC&pg=PA152&dq=%22donga%22|%22dongas%22+australia+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=-FFCT6DEFMeuiQfRiKy1BA&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22donga%22|%22dongas%22%20australia%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false page 152],
#*: '''Menzies Hotel''' ([Ph] 9024 2043; 22 Shenton St; s/d $48/65, '''donga''' $75) has old-style hotel rooms as well as - for that real goldfields experience - '''dongas''' (temporary miner′s abode, usually made from corrugated iron), and also serves all meals.
#* '''2004''', James Woodford, ''The Dog Fence'', [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=qNntO4VFNUkC&pg=PA225&dq=%22donga%22|%22dongas%22+australia+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=WVdCT6q7HoeQiAfsrsDlBA&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22donga%22|%22dongas%22%20australia%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false page 225],
#*: He not only expects his fence to be perfect, he also expects his '''dongas''' to be the best workman′s huts in Australia, and that is what they are.
#* '''2009''', [[w:David Marr (journalist)|David Marr]], ''The Ibdian Ocean Solution'', [[w:Robyn Davidson|Robyn Davidson]] (editor), ''The Best Australian Essays 2009'', [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=VfCwXaVxtdcC&pg=PA118&dq=%22donga%22|%22dongas%22+australia+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=WVdCT6q7HoeQiAfsrsDlBA&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22donga%22|%22dongas%22%20australia%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false page 118],
#*: Workers building roads in the bush sleep in '''dongas''' like these and are well paid for their discomfort.

=====Usage notes=====
* Usually used in [[outback]] Australia, especially the northwest.

